# Cloudflare Pages — HTTP headers
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Note there is deliberately no `_redirects` file. The app uses hash routing
# (#/profile, #/practice…), so every HTTP request is either "/" or a real file
# on disk. An SPA catch-all rewrite would only hide genuine 404s — a missing
# data/questions.js would come back as HTML pretending to be JavaScript, which
# is far harder to diagnose than a plain 404.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# The question bank is 3 MB and changes only when the corpus is rebuilt.
#
# The charset is stated explicitly. A classic <script> inherits the document's
# encoding only when the response says nothing, so a host that ever labelled
# this file ISO-8859-1 would render every Vietnamese diacritic as mojibake
# ("mệnh đề" → "má»‡nh Ä‘á»"). The file also keeps its UTF-8 BOM, which pins
# the decoding a second time.
/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
  Content-Type: text/javascript; charset=utf-8

# Everything else is served with must-revalidate rather than a max-age.
#
# None of these filenames are content-hashed (there is no build step to hash
# them), so any max-age at all means a redeploy reaches users late and, worse,
# in pieces: a fresh index.html next to hour-old JavaScript. The files total
# well under 200 KB and revalidation is a 304, so the cost is a round-trip.
/js/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/css/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
